{"sections":{"main":{"type":"main-article","blocks":{"title":{"type":"title","settings":{"blog_show_date":false,"blog_show_author":false}},"content":{"type":"content","settings":{}},"share":{"type":"share","settings":{"share_label":"Share"}}},"block_order":["title","content","share"],"disabled":true,"custom_css":[],"settings":{}},"rich_text_nFH3Cg":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_zAQhNR":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"Best Delay Pedals for Synths & Hardware","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_zAQhNR"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_BwkhKF":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_xiKBJU":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Delay pedals are some of the most powerful tools you can add to a synth or hardware setup. The right delay can turn a simple riff into a lush, evolving soundscape, or add subtle movement that brings a track to life. But with so many options out there, which ones actually work best for <strong>synths, drum machines, and electronic music production<\/strong>?<\/p><p>In this guide, I’ll walk you through the <strong>7 best delay pedals for synths and hardware users<\/strong>. Each one has been tested hands-on with hardware, from gritty <strong>analog delays<\/strong> to deep <strong>digital and modular-style effects<\/strong>. Whether you’re looking for warm tape-style echoes, stereo ambience, or experimental pitch-shifting textures, this list will help you find the perfect <strong>delay pedal in the context of electronic music.<\/strong><\/p><p>To address the elephant in the room upfront - yes, the Roland TR-1000 exists, but <strong>STILL <\/strong>- the <strong>Roland TR-8S<\/strong> has earned its place as one of the most powerful modern drum machines - a flexible, hands-on unit that bridges classic TR heritage with the needs and requests of modern producers. But here’s the truth: if you’re only using it as a standalone drum machine, you’re tapping into maybe <strong>20% of what it can do<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2>Where to pick up these pedals:<\/h2><p><em>** There are purchase links (for available units) throughout this Blog. Using those links would be a huge support to this channel and everything that I do:<\/em><\/p><p><em><strong>Prefer to watch instead? Here’s the video version of this blog post 👇🏼<\/strong><\/em><\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_xiKBJU"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":20,"padding_bottom":0}},"video_AyWKxj":{"type":"video","name":"t:sections.video.presets.name","settings":{"heading":"","heading_size":"h1","enable_video_looping":false,"video_url":"https:\/\/youtu.be\/04vnSSK8OE8","cover_image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Thumbnail_Paolo_Video_5_Reverb_YT.png","description":"","full_width":false,"color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_DXTYrG":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_Ceg4GB":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"1. Chase Bliss Thermae","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_Ceg4GB"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_m87Ekx":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/thrmae.jpg?v=1757627276\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_dHB3Nk":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_zXrMEB":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Mono Analog delay with digital controls<\/p><p>- The <strong>delay lines themselves are analog bucket brigade (BBD) chips<\/strong>, which give it that warm, organic character.<\/p><p>- The <strong>digital side<\/strong> handles modulation, pitch-shifting, presets, MIDI, and advanced control.<\/p><p><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: Pitch-shifting delay lines<\/p><p>Chase Bliss calls it <em>“analog heart, digital brain.”<\/em> Thermae combines analog warmth with digital pitch manipulation, giving you intervals like fourths, fifths, and octaves layered into your delay trails.<\/p><p>With two pitch shifters, a resonant low-pass filter, and even a quirky glide function, Thermae is a compact but experimental delay that can add harmonic depth or atonal textures.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Experimental producers looking for pitch-shifted, character-rich delays in a compact form.<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_zXrMEB"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_eHALKF":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_Y4YnJE":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"2. Boss DM-101 Delay Machine","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_Y4YnJE"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_XcKtUG":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/boss.jpg?v=1757627404\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_frWQJc":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_c6pyqN":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Digitally controlled analog delay (stereo)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: 12 algorithms in one pedal<\/p><p>The DM-101 takes Boss’s long history of analog delay designs and wraps them into a modern, versatile unit. With 12 modes inspired by classic Boss pedals, stereo operation, MIDI tempo sync, and rock-solid build quality, it’s like having a collection of Boss delays in one box.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Producers who want <strong>classic analog tones<\/strong> with the flexibility of awesome presets and MIDI sync.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/g1jmZ2\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/g1jmZ2\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/boss-dm-101-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/boss-dm-101-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_c6pyqN"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_gWwkyy":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_xxBgWy":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"3. Source Audio Nemesis","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_xxBgWy"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_mDtNBk":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/nemesis.jpg?v=1757627558\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_ExWAtb":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_69hJ9X":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Digital multi-algorithm delay (stereo)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: 24 delay engines in a simple interface<\/p><p>The Nemesis offers a huge range of digital delay flavors — from clean studio echoes to rhythmic patterns and pitch-shifted textures. Despite its depth, it’s extremely intuitive, with dedicated knobs for mix, feedback, tone, and modulation.<\/p><p>It’s also highly MIDI-friendly, making tempo sync with synths easy.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Hardware users who want a <strong>wide palette of digital delays<\/strong> without deep menu diving.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/0ZWgLE\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/0ZWgLE\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/source-audio-nemesis-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/source-audio-nemesis-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_69hJ9X"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_RX6L6c":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_mkNEyy":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"4. Empress Echosystem","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_mkNEyy"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_Yfq4Jr":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/echo.jpg?v=1757627725\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_XcQhbt":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_m9pgbB":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Dual-engine digital delay (stereo)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: Run two delays at once<\/p><p>The Echosystem lets you layer and blend two different delay algorithms in parallel, series, or split left\/right. This opens up endless possibilities for ambient textures, rhythmic interplay, or simply stacking complementary delays.<\/p><p>It also includes delay + reverb presets and CV control for modular integration.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Ambient and experimental producers who want <strong>layered delay textures<\/strong>.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/m5AL6a\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/m5AL6a\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/empreess-echosystem-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/empreess-echosystem-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_m9pgbB"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_cBfziX":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_FtJqNa":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"5. Red Panda Particle","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_FtJqNa"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_pkyxjJ":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/red.jpg?v=1757627868\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_EmgBCW":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_hDReTz":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Granular & pitch-shifting delay (stereo, digital)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: Granular delay<\/p><p>The Particle is designed for <strong>glitchy, unpredictable textures<\/strong>. It slices incoming audio into grains and replays them in randomized or pitch-shifted patterns. You can choose between delay-based or pitch-based modes, with plenty of modulation to push sounds into glitchy chaos.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Sound designers who want <strong>granular and glitch textures<\/strong> beyond traditional delays.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/rQ0BXD\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/rQ0BXD\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/red-panda-particle-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/red-panda-particle-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_hDReTz"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_UUC3WQ":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_wAcHUf":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"6. Meris LVX","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_wAcHUf"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_3QJrVG":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/lvx.jpg?v=1757628078\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_WdgirW":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_AwrUDi":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Modular digital delay workstation (stereo)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: Modular patching within a pedal<\/p><p>The LVX takes delay to the extreme, letting you design signal chains using modules like pitch, filters, modulation, and dynamics. Its assignable surface knobs make it hands-on, while deep editing lets you build entirely new delay engines.<\/p><p>It’s MIDI and CV ready, making it one of the most future-proof pedals for electronic musicians.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Producers who want <strong>deep sound design potential<\/strong> and a pedal that goes far beyond delay.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/anL4eY\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/anL4eY\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/meris-lvx-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/meris-lvx-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_AwrUDi"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":20}},"rich_text_4BQA7n":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"heading_HVmdwi":{"type":"heading","settings":{"heading":"7. Strymon Deco V2","heading_size":"h1"}}},"block_order":["heading_HVmdwi"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"center","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}},"custom_liquid_cR9iGJ":{"type":"custom-liquid","name":"t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name","settings":{"custom_liquid":"<div style=\"\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  width: 100%;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0 20px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n\">\n  <img\n    src=\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0904\/5927\/5539\/files\/deco.jpg?v=1757628175\"\n    style=\"\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 1000px;\n      height: auto;\n      display: block;\n    \"\n    alt=\"\"\n  >\n<\/div>","color_scheme":"","padding_top":12,"padding_bottom":12}},"rich_text_7Dpbxe":{"type":"rich-text","blocks":{"text_a6Wjz4":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Type<\/strong>: Tape delay & saturation (stereo, digital)<br\/><strong>Unique feature<\/strong>: Tape-style delay + saturation in one<\/p><p>The Deco is all about vibe. On one side you get warm tape-style delay, slapback, chorus, and flanger. On the other, lush tape saturation adds richness to any synth or drum machine.<\/p><p>It may not be as versatile as the bigger multi-engine pedals, but it delivers character in spades.<\/p><p>👉 <strong>Best for<\/strong>: Adding <strong>warm tape character<\/strong> and vintage-inspired delays to synths.<\/p><p><strong>Affiliate links: <\/strong><\/p><p>🇺🇸: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/Kj1rRy\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/sweetwater.sjv.io\/Kj1rRy\">Sweetwater<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🌍: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/strymon-deco-thomann\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/strymon-deco-thomann\">Thomann<\/a> ]<\/p><p>🇨🇦: [ <a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/moogaudio\">Moog Audio<\/a> ]<\/p>"}},"text_rUXVM6":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><em><strong>Thanks as always for your support  - <\/strong><\/em><a href=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/blogs\/home\" title=\"https:\/\/liamkillen.store\/blogs\/home\"><em><strong>here<\/strong><\/em><\/a><em><strong> is a link to other blogs you may also enjoy.<\/strong><\/em><\/p>"}}},"block_order":["text_a6Wjz4","text_rUXVM6"],"name":"t:sections.rich-text.presets.name","settings":{"desktop_content_position":"center","content_alignment":"left","color_scheme":"","full_width":true,"padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":52}}},"order":["main","rich_text_nFH3Cg","rich_text_BwkhKF","video_AyWKxj","rich_text_DXTYrG","custom_liquid_m87Ekx","rich_text_dHB3Nk","rich_text_eHALKF","custom_liquid_XcKtUG